<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at -0.87 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at -0.87 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty  at 3.4660 to the dollar, down from 3.4630 on Thursday and at 1.8720  to the mark, up from 1.8905, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 0.87 percent below  the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Thursday's  fix at -1.27 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
